        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ac545da3-7495-516c-805d-eed1888015c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edith Bouvier Beale, Little Edie, Edith Ewing Bouvier, Big Edie, Drew Barrymore, Jessica Lange, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Jacqueline Kennedy, Ken Howard, Phelan Beale, Michael Sucsy\n- Works: Grey Gardens\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Roles: attorney, sportsman\n\nFacts:\n- Phelan Beale was born on May 23, 1881, and died on June 12, 1956.\n- Phelan Beale was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City.\n- Phelan Beale was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, who was an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\n- Grey Gardens is an HBO film about Edith Bouvier Beale, known as Little Edie, and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier, known as Big Edie.\n- Drew Barrymore played Little Edie in Grey Gardens, and Jessica Lange played Big Edie.\n- Jeanne Tripplehorn co-starred in Grey Gardens as Jacqueline Kennedy, who was Little Edie’s cousin.\n- Ken Howard co-starred in Grey Gardens as Phelan Beale, who was Little Edie’s father.\n- Michael Sucsy is best known for creating the HBO film Grey Gardens.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "22915e4a-c9e6-550d-a147-908832ac2d8f",
        "text": "Page: Grey Gardens (2009 film). Sentence: Grey Gardens is an HBO film about the lives of Edith Bouvier Beale/\"Little Edie\", played by Drew Barrymore, and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier/\"Big Edie\", played by Jessica Lange.\nPage: Grey Gardens (2009 film). Sentence: Co-stars include Jeanne Tripplehorn as Jacqueline Kennedy (Little Edie's cousin) and Ken Howard as Phelan Beale (Little Edie's father).\nPage: Phelan Beale. Sentence: Phelan Beale (May 23, 1881 – June 12, 1956) was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City who was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\nPage: Michael Sucsy. Sentence: He is best known for creating the HBO film \"Grey Gardens\".",
